      "What could tokenisation mean for the future of money, markets and the UK economy?\n\nIn the latest Barclays Viewpoint, we explore how tokenisation is moving from concept to practical application, and why its impact could reach far beyond financial services.",
      "2026 Wimble-Done! 🎾🍓 Here are some of the unmissable moments we served up at SW19, in our fourth year as Official Banking Partner of Wimbledon:\n\n· The Clubhouse by Barclays has delivered more than 41,000 customer and fan interactions, bringing people closer to the game through player appearances, rewards, giveaways and interactive experiences.\n\n· We provided over 24,000 free strawberries and cream for our customers.\n\n· The Wimbledon Ticket Resale scheme, supported by Barclays, has already raised almost £280,000 for the Wimbledon Foundation.\n\n· At the Wimbledon Foundation Kiosk, more than 10,0…",
      "Ten years on from the Brexit referendum, the debate is shifting from what has happened to what comes next. In the latest edition of The Barclays Viewpoint, we explore the ideas, behaviours and innovations that could shape the UK’s future.\n\n📈 Rhiannon Price examines whether “Baby Bonds” could help broaden investment participation and support UK capital markets.\n🎙️ Jack Meaning and Patrick Coffey discuss the economic model that could define Britain’s next decade.\n💷 Vim Maru explores why households have rebuilt financial resilience, but confidence is not yet translating into action. \n⚡ Bernard L…",
      "Digital assets are one of the most talked about developments in the financial landscape today. To help you understand the future of money, and the potential opportunities digital assets pose for customers, clients and the economy, start here.\n\n🎥 To watch the full video on YouTube follow the link in comments.",
      "🍓☀️ A day at Wimbledon got me thinking...\n\nSuccess doesn't happen overnight, whether you're on Centre Court or building your career. 🎾💚\n\nIt's about resilience, continuous learning and making the most of every opportunity that comes your way.\n\nWhat lessons from sport have helped you in your career? 👇✨",
      "Why is the UK losing ground as a hub for foreign investment and how can it attract more?\n\nThat's the question explored in Barclays' policy report \"Building an investment-led growth model: A new blueprint for attracting global capital into the UK.” We sat down with the report's author, Ravi Prasad, to unpack its findings.\n\nDownload the report via link in comments and check out @barclayspolicygroup on Substack to read more from Ravi.",
      "🎉✨ How does it feel to be recognised for making a difference?\nOur recent Citizenship, Inclusion & Opportunity Awards celebrated colleagues from across the globe who make an ongoing impact in their communities. We caught up with some of the finalists and winners to hear their stories and reflect on what this recognition means to them 💙 \n#citizenshipinclusionopportunityawards",
      "🎾💚 Looking back, some of the biggest moments in our careers came from taking a chance on ourselves.\n\nWhether it was stepping outside our comfort zones, saying yes to a new opportunity or learning from a challenge, those moments helped shape the paths we're on today. ✨🌱\n\nWhat's been your career match point moment? 🎾👇"
    ]
  },
